 Concept #9 — Trigram Similarity                                                                                                              
                                                                                                                                             
  You already met the bug today. Quick recap:                                                                                                  
                                                                                                                                               
  - akash wrote Dhurandhar 2025 Blockbuster (correct spelling)                                                                                 
  - aditya wrote Dhruandhar in japan (typo — Dhru not Dhur)                                                                                    
                                                                                                                                             
  A reader searches dhurandhar. Full-text search finds 1 post. The other one is invisible because the stemmer treats dhurandhar and dhruandhar
  as completely different tokens. Same bug shape we keep meeting — content quietly missing.

  ---
  Beat 1 — how trigram works (intuition only, no code)

  Take any word and break it into overlapping 3-character chunks (called trigrams). That's it.

  "dhurandhar" → ["dhu", "hur", "ura", "ran", "and", "ndh", "dha", "har"]
  "dhruandhar" → ["dhr", "hru", "rua", "uan", "and", "ndh", "dha", "har"]

  Now count shared chunks vs total chunks across both words:

  ┌───────┬──────────────────┬──────────────────┐
  │ Chunk │ In "dhurandhar"? │ In "dhruandhar"? │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ dhu   │ ✓                │ ✗                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ hur   │ ✓                │ ✗                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ ura   │ ✓                │ ✗                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ dhr   │ ✗                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ hru   │ ✗                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ rua   │ ✗                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ uan   │ ✗                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ ran   │ ✓                │ ✗                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ and   │ ✓                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ ndh   │ ✓                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ dha   │ ✓                │ ✓                │
  ├───────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────┤
  │ har   │ ✓                │ ✓                │
  └───────┴──────────────────┴──────────────────┘

  4 chunks shared out of 12 total → similarity ≈ 0.33. Above the typical threshold of 0.3, so they match.

  That's the entire algorithm. No stemming, no language rules, no dictionaries — just pure character-overlap math. Which means it works on any
  word in any language, including made-up ones, names, brand names, typos.

  ---
  The mental model — full-text vs trigram, side by side:

  ┌─────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┐
  │                     │                    Full-text search                     │      Trigram similarity       │
  ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
  │ What it understands │ Meaning (running = run, movies = movie)                 │ Spelling (djangoo ≈ django)   │
  ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
  │ Breaks text into    │ Words (after lowercasing, stemming)                     │ 3-char chunks                 │
  ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
  │ Wins at             │ "the reader meant the same concept, in different words" │ "the reader misspelled it"    │
  ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
  │ Loses at            │ Typos and brand names it's never seen                   │ Synonyms ("car" vs "vehicle") │
  ├─────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
  │ Production answer   │ Combine both with an OR                                 │ Combine both with an OR       │
  └─────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘
